@inject IJSRuntime JS

@*
    The way back, and it is the way you came.

    Every page used to send you to the landing, which is only right when the landing is where you
    were — and it usually is not: you reach the review from a finished sitting or from an import,
    and being returned to the front door from there loses the domain's context and reads as being
    thrown out. So this steps back through the history the client actually walked.

    It falls back to the landing when there is nothing to step back to, which is the case that
    matters for a page opened straight from a bookmark or a pasted URL: browser back would leave
    Alembic altogether.
*@

<a class="back" href="" @onclick="GoBackAsync" @onclick:preventDefault>&larr; back</a>

@code {
    private async Task GoBackAsync() => await JS.InvokeVoidAsync("alembicBack");
}
